From 57ba6af8826601da9f61b7c86f18ec829b9f2b5b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: CyberAshven <130158492+CyberAshven@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 11:59:12 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] feat(node): build the input prefix filter when asked and keep
 nothing for it, its filter headers an option

node.input_prefix_filters now serves getcfilters for filter type 2 alone:
each filter is built from its block in the service of the peer that asked,
as for the regular filter, and nothing is kept for it, in memory or on
disk; nothing grows with the chain for it. getcfheaders and getcfcheckpt
for type 2 then get no answer, as for a type the node does not serve, and a
wallet takes the filter hashes from the filters.

node.input_prefix_filter_headers (off by default, needs
node.input_prefix_filters) keeps what the previous commits kept: the filter
hash and filter header of every block in input_prefix_filter_headers, read
and written by the compact filter index, and serves getcfheaders and
getcfcheckpt for type 2 from them. compact_filter_index_files names what
the index keeps in each mode, and the node runs the index with it.

Turned off again, the file is neither read nor written; turned on again, it
is taken up where it stopped.

Tests: by default the index keeps the regular filter alone, no type 2 file
is created, type 2 filters are built and its filter headers are not
answered; on one database the headers mode, then the default with blocks
connected meanwhile (the file untouched, no headers answered), then the
headers mode again, which takes the file up to the tip; the parser.
